      "notes": "Layout: the problems PDF (8 pp.) has a cover (p.1, sponsor logos, not cropped), instructions (p.2, stored in paper.documentNotes), a list of constants (p.3, stored in paper.documentNotes) and three questions on pp.4-8. The solutions PDF (24 pp.) repeats cover/instructions/constants (pp.1-3) and each question statement (sol. pp.4-5, 11, 19-20) before the official solutions (sol. pp.6-10, 12-18, 21-24). The restated statements match the problems PDF except that the On Ice equation U(r)=C/r^6 is numbered (1) in the problems PDF and (18) in the solutions PDF; the solutions-PDF instructions are an updated version (e.g. 'must submit', 'Teams that do not submit rough work will be disqualified') - the problems-PDF version is used. Each top-level 'Theory Question' has printed sub-sections A/B (C/D in Q3) whose printed sub-tasks (A.1, A.2, ..., D.2) are the parts; section headings with their marks are kept in the statement / statementAfter text. The catalogue expected about 27 sub-tasks; the paper prints 24 (Q1: 7, Q2: 4, Q3: 13). Point markers are removed from part statements (they are in points); in Q1 B.1-B.3 they are printed without unit ('[1.5]', '[2]', '[1.5]'). Part points sum to the printed 10 marks per question; paper total is not printed (totalPoints null). timeLimitMin 2880 is derived from the printed window 'August 23, 12:00 AM UTC to August 24, 11:59 PM UTC' (2 full days). Round: printed 'Invitational Contest' / 'Invitational Round', 'Part I'; round set to null because the controlled vocabulary has no such value (catalogue says 'theory').\nPrinted source errors kept verbatim: problems p.7 'the stakes are perfectly vertical' (skates); p.7 'a layer of liquid layer of height h'; p.2 'submit up 10 MB'; p.6 Q2 A.2/A.3 refer to 'part (a)' and 'part (b)' although the parts are labelled (A.1)/(A.2); p.8 'this criteria'; Q3 uses nu for the dynamic viscosity of water with units kg/(m s). Solutions: sol. p.6 marking scheme 'relating theta_1 and theta_2' (the angles are theta_0 and theta_1) and the quote style '”refraction”'; sol. p.8 (d) 'the maximum value of beta has R = 0' as printed; sol. p.8 Erratum: the official solution itself states that the image-loop construction for (b)-(d) is wrong and that full points for (b)-(d) were given for the key sphere-plane image idea - answers for A.2-A.4 are marked accordingly; sol. p.18 eq. (15) prints 'integral u_phi dm' (not squared) on the right-hand side; sol. pp.21-22 'Clausius-Clayperon' (Clapeyron); sol. p.22 'h ∝ 1/(T - T_m)^{-1/3}' and 'below 0.088°C' (without minus sign) as printed; sol. p.23 'C = (T_m - T_0)/sqrt(2 pi)' while eq. (42) gives sqrt(pi) C = difference, 'Equating this with (18)' (refers to the problem's equation number, apparently meaning eq. (35)); sol. p.24 'to lowest order in C_1/C_2' and eq. (50) f = 2 nu w v (C_2/C_1) sqrt(L) as printed; sol. p.17 team name quoted as ”rotting crustaceans”. Red point markers '(0.2)' etc. in the On Ice solution are rendered bold. Q2 solution figures 1-5 are photos of handwritten sketches with handwritten explanations; the handwriting is inside the crops (summarised in alt), not transcribed. No illegible spots. Hyperlinks (google form, this form, here, IPhO formula sheet) are plain text in the instructions. Repaired 2026-10-04 from the independent verification (docs/verification/2026-10-0*-round*) of the agent:opus-5-5 (2026-09-22) transcription: sol. p.23 eq. (38) denominator restored to the printed sqrt{D},t^{3/2} (the radical covers only D).",
